Reason: The provided class implements an asynchronous RxJava operator that schedules work on a Scheduler. Benchmarking such asynchronous, side‑effect‑driven code with JMH is non‑trivial and generally not appropriate for a simple microbenchmark. Proper measurement would require coordination with the Scheduler, waiting for completion, and handling thread‑pool overhead, which falls outside the typical scope of JMH throughput benchmarks. Existing RxJava test suites already cover functional correctness and performance characteristics of this operator. Hence, generating a JMH benchmark is unnecessary.